    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a disposable-domain blocklist rule to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, rejecting with **400** when the owner's email domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor conventions and keeping each piece where it belongs:\n\n1. **`OwnerEmails`** (the shared email rule set) \u2014 extended with `domainOf(email)` and `isDisposable(email)` plus the blocklist constant, so the disposable-domain rule lives alongside the existing presence/validity/normalize rules rather than being scattered.\n\n2. **`RejectDisposableOwnerEmail`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility `Reject<E>` step (matching the existing `RejectFullOwnerCity` etc.) that throws when a present email's domain is disposable; an absent email is a no-op.\n\n3. **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** + **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** \u2014 a dedicated checked exception and 400 handler built via the shared `ProblemDetails`, mirroring the per-rule exception pattern already in use (I deliberately did not overload `InvalidEmailException`, whose contract is *syntactic* validity \u2014 a disposable address is syntactically valid).\n\n4. **Wiring** \u2014 the escalation YAML (`...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml`) and a `rejectDisposableEmail` step inserted after `normalizeEmail` in `owners.POST.yml`, so the domain is already normalized/lower-cased when the check runs, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) passes.",
